class_name Guide
extends RefCounted
## The guide book: short pages that explain how the game works. Pages unlock
## as you play and pop up once (you can skip them). Skipped or not, they stay
## readable in Codex > Guide.
## [b], [color] and the like work in the text (it's shown as rich text).

const PAGES := [
	{"id": "welcome", "title": "Welcome to Solaria", "text": "Your hero fights on their own, one room after another. Every floor has 3 fights.\n\n[b]Tap the monster[/b] to hit it yourself for extra damage.\n\nThe dungeon is split into [b]zones of 50 floors[/b]. Each zone has 5 areas of 10 floors, a [b]mid boss on floor 25[/b] and a [b]zone boss on floor 50[/b].\n\nYou can't play while the game is closed, so nothing happens when you're away. Take your time."},
	{"id": "gear", "title": "Gear and rarity", "text": "Monsters drop gear for 6 slots: Weapon, Off Hand, Helmet, Chest, Legs and Feet.\n\nRarity goes [color=#bbbbbb]Common[/color], [color=#4ade80]Uncommon[/color], [color=#60a5fa]Rare[/color], [color=#c084fc]Epic[/color], [color=#fb923c]Legendary[/color]. Every Legendary has a special effect.\n\nBosses can drop [color=#fbbf24]Uniques[/color], and every monster has one [color=#ff6b9d]Signature[/color] item it drops once in 1,000 kills.\n\nTap or hover any item to compare it with what you're wearing. [b]Equip Best[/b] in the Gear tab puts on your strongest items."},
	{"id": "stats", "title": "Building your hero", "text": "Every level gives you [b]5 stat points[/b] for 8 stats:\n\n[b]STR[/b] Attack and some HP.  [b]VIT[/b] HP and Defense.\n[b]AGI[/b] dodge, extra swings, striking first.  [b]DEX[/b] crit and double strike.\n[b]INT[/b] skill damage and cooldowns.  [b]WIS[/b] healing, regen and status resist.\n[b]LUK[/b] loot, gold, crit damage and events.  [b]CHA[/b] shop prices, charm, party and pet.\n\nThe [color=#e8b14a]SUGGESTED[/color] chip shows your class's build. [b]Spend on my build[/b] does it for you, and [b]Auto[/b] keeps doing it every level. Respec tomes reset your points, and you can save up to 3 builds (stats, skills and gear) in Character > Hero.\n\nYour [b]special stat[/b] doesn't take points: it grows from what you do (the card says what)."},

	{"id": "abilities", "title": "Skills and ability stones", "text": "Your class starts with one active and one passive skill. More come from [b]ability stones[/b]: about 1 in 100 monsters drops one, rare monsters drop them more, and bosses always do.\n\nEquip up to [b]3 active[/b] skills (slots open at levels 1, 10, 25) and [b]5 passive[/b] skills (levels 1, 5, 15, 30, 45) in Character > Skills.\n\nLeave [b]Auto[/b] on and active skills fire by themselves, or press them yourself."},

	{"id": "death", "title": "When you fall", "text": "Falling costs everything you carried in: the gold on you, your bag and the gear you were wearing. You wake at the start of that 25-floor stretch (floor 1, 26, 51...).\n\nThe Bank, the Vault and the Mailbox are always safe. Leave the dungeon after any cleared floor to keep what you found.\n\nHardcore heroes only get one life."},
	{"id": "shop", "title": "The shop", "text": "Spend gold on potions, gear, elixirs and a bigger bag.\n\nThe shop and its featured deal get new stock every 25 floors (after each boss). You can also pay a little to restock early."},
	{"id": "craft", "title": "Crafting and materials", "text": "Sell or salvage gear you don't need. Salvaging gives [b]scrap[/b], which upgrades and rerolls your best items.\n\nEach zone has its own [b]material[/b]. You get them from bosses (lots), Rare or better monsters, dungeon events and by salvaging Epic or Legendary gear. Materials craft [color=#2dd4bf]Set[/color] items and bigger bags."},
	{"id": "zones", "title": "Zones and bosses", "text": "Every area adds one creature of its own, so each 10 floors feels a bit different and drops different things.\n\nThe [b]mid boss[/b] (floor 25) and [b]zone boss[/b] (floor 50) drop 3 items, 5-8 materials and sometimes a Unique.\n\nYou can travel back to fight any boss you've reached from the Floors button. A boss needs a short rest (15-30 seconds) between fights."},
	{"id": "monster_tiers", "title": "Rare monsters", "text": "Monsters come in tiers: [color=#cbd5e1]Common[/color], [color=#4ade80]Uncommon[/color], [color=#60a5fa]Rare[/color], [color=#c084fc]Epic[/color], [color=#fb923c]Legendary[/color] and [color=#ff4d6d]Mythic[/color]. Their name color and glow tell you which.\n\nThe rarer they are, the bigger and tougher they get, with 1 to 4 [b]modifiers[/b] like Swift, Vampiric or Shielded. They also pay out much better: more gold, more and better loot, and materials.\n\nOnly about 1 in 200 monsters is Mythic. Hardcore heroes meet rare monsters more often."},
	{"id": "bestiary", "title": "The Bestiary", "text": "Every monster you meet goes in the Bestiary (Codex tab). It shows how many you've killed, what they like to drop and their real drop odds.\n\nKill enough of one monster and you get a permanent bonus against it: [b]10, 100, 500 and 1,000 kills[/b] give more damage and gold.\n\nEach monster also has a Signature item. You can see its odds, but not what it is, until you find it."},
	{"id": "events", "title": "Dungeon events", "text": "About every 10 floors something unusual happens:\n\n[b]Treasure goblin[/b]: it doesn't fight back, but it runs away after a few turns. Catch it for a pile of loot.\n[b]Monster horde[/b]: 5 weaker monsters in a row, with a chest at the end.\n[b]Cursed shrine[/b]: accept its curse for tougher monsters but much better loot, or walk past."},
	{"id": "merchant", "title": "The wandering merchant", "text": "After each boss you might meet a wandering merchant at the fork in the road. He sells Epic and Legendary gear, mystery boxes and rare scrolls:\n\n[b]Scroll of Luck[/b]: better loot for a while.\n[b]Hunter's Scroll[/b]: rare monsters show up much more often.\n[b]Boss Key[/b]: bosses are ready to fight again right away."},
	{"id": "uniques", "title": "Uniques and Signatures", "text": "[color=#fbbf24]Uniques[/color] drop from bosses. Every boss you beat without one raises the chance for the next.\n\n[color=#ff6b9d]Signature[/color] items are much rarer: each monster has exactly one, and it drops once in 1,000 kills. There's no pity timer. Most players will only ever see a few. Your finds go in Codex > Collection."},
	{"id": "specs", "title": "Your Evolution Tree", "text": "Every class grows on an [b]Evolution Tree[/b]: at [b]level 15[/b] it splits in two, at [b]level 35[/b] each of those splits in two, and at [b]level 60[/b] in two again. You pick each step in Character > Class. Classes you haven't reached show as [b]???[/b].\n\nEvery evolution teaches a [color=#ff6b9d]signature skill[/color] for your 4th skill slot.\n\nYour deeds limit you: every class is [color=#86efac]Good[/color], Neutral or [color=#f87171]Evil[/color]. Faith above +25 makes you Good, below -25 Evil. A Good hero can't take an Evil class, an Evil hero can't take a Good one, and a Neutral hero can take either."},

	{"id": "heroes", "title": "More heroes", "text": "You've unlocked another hero slot! You can have up to 3 heroes (the 2nd unlocks at floor 25, the 3rd at floor 50).\n\nSwitch heroes from the title screen. Regular heroes share a [b]stash[/b] (Items > Stash), so you can pass gear between them. The Bestiary, achievements and bounties are shared by all your heroes."},
	{"id": "skills", "title": "The Skill Book", "text": "Every skill you find goes in your Skill Book (Character > Skills).\n\nA [b]duplicate stone[/b] ranks a skill up (max 5). A stone for a skill that's already max rank turns into [b]dust[/b], and dust crafts any skill you want, even ones you've never found.\n\nEvery skill has [b]tags[/b] (Fire, Holy, Blade...). Skills that share a tag with your class hit 15% harder, and the tag you use most decides your evolution at level 35."},
	{"id": "party", "title": "Your party", "text": "Once you have more than one Regular hero, bring up to 2 of them along (Character > Party).\n\nCompanions fight with their own gear, stats and skills. Healers heal whoever is hurt most, and monsters aim mostly at [b]tanks[/b] (Warriors and Knights). A fallen companion gets back up on the next floor.\n\nMonsters get tougher with a bigger party, but you get extra loot and all your heroes level up together. The party also shares one skill book."},
	{"id": "paths", "title": "Unique classes and ranks", "text": "Your class evolves at levels 15, 35 and 60, and you won't know into what until you get there. The level 60 classes are [b]unique classes[/b], each with a rank (C, B, A, S, SS or [color=#fde047]God[/color]) and a special stat that grows as you fight.\n\nRank is fighting strength. Some say the way you fight can open paths no one chooses on purpose."},
	{"id": "wheel", "title": "Fortune's Wheel", "text": "Town > Wheel lets you gamble an item. Win and it comes back [b]one rarity higher[/b] (its upgrades stay). Lose and it's gone for good.\n\nThe rarer the item, the worse the odds: Common 55%, Uncommon 40%, Rare 25%, Epic 10%. There's a small gold fee per spin. Locked items, Legendary and better can't go on the wheel.\n\nTip: rerolling in the Craft tab is safer (you keep the item if it fails) but its odds are lower."},
	{"id": "races", "title": "Your race and its power", "text": "Every race has its own [b]racial power[/b]: Divine Power for Angels, Demonic Energy for Demons, Forgecraft for Dwarves and so on. It grows from playing your race's way (the Race tab says how), and you can put stat points into it (0.1 each). Every point gives a small bonus.\n\nEnough of it, plus a high enough level, lets you [b]awaken[/b]: Angels grow more pairs of wings, Demons climb to royalty, Elves seek the World Tree's blessing. Some ranks also need a key: an item from somewhere special, or a trial fight. Awakening changes how you look too."},
	{"id": "escape", "title": "Running and sparing", "text": "Not every fight has to be fought. Press [b]Run[/b] to try to get away: your [b]AGI[/b] helps, rarer monsters are harder to escape, and you can't run from bosses. If you fail, the monster gets a free hit. If you get away, you get no XP or loot from it.\n\nWhen a monster is nearly beaten (under 25% HP) you can [b]Spare[/b] it. It slinks away and remembers you."},
	{"id": "reputation", "title": "Friends and enemies", "text": "Every race has an opinion of you, from [color=#dc2626]Hated[/color] to [color=#e8b14a]Exalted[/color]. Your own race starts friendly; its rivals start hostile (Angels and Demons, Elves and Orcs, Dwarves and Goblins, Humans and the Undead).\n\nKilling a race's people lowers it; sparing them, letting them pass on the road and doing their quests raises it. Helping one race annoys its rivals.\n\nFriends trade with you, show you hidden paths and help on the road. People who hate you hit harder."},
	{"id": "realms", "title": "The realms", "text": "Below floor 250 the World Tree's roots crack open into the homelands of the races. Floors 251-500 are [b]5 realms[/b], and you choose the order: after each ruler falls, portals open to the realms you haven't seen. Your race, faith and road open some and lock others.\n\nEach realm plays differently: the Hushwood's mist makes attacks miss, the Glimmer Court hides what monsters really are, the forge-heat of the Ironroot Deeps burns, the Gilded Spire judges your soul and the Cinder Abyss's hellfire feeds your lifesteal.\n\nEach realm also has its own event, a camp with that race's merchant and quest board, a set, uniques and secrets. The Race tab shows how much of each realm you've done."},
	{"id": "transform", "title": "Transformations", "text": "Some things change you for good. A [b]vampire's bite[/b] can turn a Human, a [b]cursed hound's bite[/b] can make a Werewolf (at the next full moon), an Angel whose faith falls too far becomes a [b]Fallen Angel[/b], and a dark caster can become a [b]Lich[/b].\n\nVampires and Werewolves can be cured with a long quest, if they want to be. Fallen Angels and Liches are forever: only starting the hero over undoes it."},
	{"id": "hidden", "title": "Hidden classes", "text": "Some classes are secret. You unlock them by [b]how you play[/b], not by choosing them.\n\n[color=#4ade80]Discoveries[/color] are easy to stumble into. [color=#38bdf8]Masteries[/color] take level 60, a long feat and a trial. [color=#e8b14a]Legends[/color] take level 100 or more and pull from everything you've done; some can only be held by one hero on your account.\n\nA hidden class sits on top of your class: you keep your class and skills and gain its title, bonuses and its own special stat. Nobody can tell you how to find one. Listen to what people say by the fire."},
	{"id": "bounties", "title": "Bounties and achievements", "text": "The Codex has daily and weekly [b]bounties[/b]: small goals like \"defeat 40 monsters in the Mossy Hollows\". Finish them for gold and materials.\n\nThere are also 87 [b]achievements[/b]. Each gives a small reward, and some give a title you can show next to your name."},
	{"id": "elements", "title": "Elements and statuses", "text": "Monsters can be [b]weak[/b] or [b]resistant[/b] to elements: Fire, Ice, Lightning, Poison, Holy and Dark. The chips under a monster's name tell you. Weak takes extra damage, resistant takes less.\n\nStatuses combo: hit a [b]chilled[/b] monster with Ice to freeze it, hit a [b]frozen[/b] one hard to shatter it, Lightning on a wet or chilled foe conducts, and Poison stacks.\n\nElite monsters have modifiers like Venomous, Frigid, Explosive or Regenerating. Every boss fights its own way: shields, minions, breath, enrage timers, or a [b]crushing blow[/b] it winds up for a turn. Hit it with a skill during the wind-up to stagger it.\n\nIf you fall, a [b]death recap[/b] shows what hit you and a tip."},
	{"id": "milestones", "title": "Milestones, hazards and curses", "text": "Every 10th floor of a zone is a [b]milestone[/b]: its last fight is a Champion, and beating it gives a chest and a [b]checkpoint[/b] you can travel back to.\n\nSome floors have a [b]hazard[/b] (fog, floods, darkness and more) that changes the fight for a floor.\n\nFrom best floor 20 you can take [b]curses[/b] in the Floors menu: harder fights for more XP and loot. Turn them off any time."},
	{"id": "pets", "title": "Your companion", "text": "From level 5 a companion joins you. It fights beside you, grows with you and [b]evolves[/b] through 4 stages. Name it and rest it in the Party tab. CHA makes it stronger."},
]

static func has_page(id: String) -> bool:
	return not page(id).is_empty()

static func page(id: String) -> Dictionary:
	for p in PAGES:
		if p["id"] == id:
			return p
	return {}
